Package: latd
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: LAT (Local Area Transport) server
 latd offers LAT services to terminal servers such as DEC's DECservers and
 connects to LAT services elsewhere on the LAN (llogin). latcp configures the
 running daemon; /etc/latd.conf is run as a shell script of latcp commands
 when latd starts.
 .
 This build offers no default login service: a service exists only once
 /etc/latd.conf adds one.
